Subject: GoldenEye's guns at 120 FPS: the shot's recoil no longer flickers

GitHub issue 3 (Kode-Z): under 120 Hz every GoldenEye gun - GE Plus, Goldfinger
64 and TND64, N64 and XBLA art alike - alternated frame by frame between two
poses for the length of its fire animation after a shot; 60 Hz was smooth and
Perfect Dark's own guns were fine at both. Measured on a scratch clang oracle
(Dam, PP7, a forced trigger tap, --fixed-fps 120 against --fixed-step, the
per-frame hand state and the gun's matrices logged): the hand's state and
recoil curve (bgun0f09aba4()) were smooth at 120, but the gun model's matrices
jumped by about (0, -6, +7) on every frame drawn between two animation frames
(frac 0.5) and came back on the next (frac 0), for the 50 frames of the
animation. Those frames are the ones upstream's high-framerate pass sends
through the C path (bgunGunTweensAll(), set var8005efb0_2/var8005efd8_2), and
GoldenEye's own model in the hand - which plays its host's animation - is
posed there about 9 units from where the fast path (modelasm00018680()) puts
it: forcing the C path at 60 FPS puts it there on every frame, at whole frames
too. Perfect Dark's guns pose the same on both paths, which is why only
GoldenEye's flickered.

GoldenEye's own model in the hand (gegunsOwnModelInUse(), which is also what
the release's gun is skinned onto in the XBLA look) keeps the fast path above
60 FPS, as it has at 60: tweened rotations at the frames between, measured
smooth and monotonic through the PP7's shot. bgunGunTweensAll() is never true
at 60 or 30 FPS (animquarter stays 0 there), so that path is unchanged. Not
iOS-guarded: desktop has the same bug at any rate above 60; one for upstream.

--- a/src/game/bondgun.c
+++ b/src/game/bondgun.c
@@ -774,6 +774,16 @@
  */
 static bool bgunGunTweensAll(struct hand *hand)
 {
+	// (overlay 0064: not GoldenEye's own model in the hand, which plays its
+	// host's animation. The C path (modelUpdateMatrices()) poses that model
+	// about 9 units from where the fast path does - the whole gun and hand,
+	// at a whole frame too - so above 60 FPS every frame drawn between two
+	// jumped and the next snapped back: a GoldenEye gun's shot flickered
+	// between two poses at 120 FPS (issue 3). The fast path, as at 60.)
+	if (gegunsOwnModelInUse(hand->gset.weaponnum)) {
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	return hand->animquarter > 0 && hand->gunmodel.anim && hand->gunmodel.anim->frac != 0.0f;
 }
 #endif
